}     1	# Honest-churn arm: plan (draft 6, 2026-11-11; for internal review; no spend yet)
     2	
     3	**Why.** The Fable 5.2 fresh review (problem 4, `docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md`; triage
     4	`docs/paper/fable52-triage.md`): in both tests the nine honest opponents never replace their identities, so after the
     5	start a new identity almost always belongs to the deviating provider. This arm lets the honest opponents replace their
     6	identities and measures how R3's results change. The author asked on 2026-11-10 to "run all necessary sims"; nothing
     7	runs before this plan has internal consensus and the reservation is recorded in the budget ledger.
     8	
     9	**Status.** Draft 6. Exploratory follow-up outside the registered protocol, specified after the second test's results
    10	were seen. Not an independent replication.
    11	
    12	**Changes from draft 3** (internal review round 3, `docs/revision/roster/{sol,astra}-churn-plan-r3.md`, both reject; and
    13	the cross-cutting rules of the author and the reset plan):
    14	1. The cost admission runs again after the memory preflight chooses the workers; the first admission includes the
    15	   preflight's serial tasks; the chosen worker limit is kept for every later stage, including the diagnostics.
    16	2. The preflight runs real tasks (one evaluate task per rule, one doubling task) in child processes, takes the largest
    17	   peak with a 25 percent margin for markets, rules and winners, and keeps their records; doubling is measured itself.
    18	3. The pod gate requires bit identity (`--require-identical`, the semantics of the reset driver's `pod_gate_ok`; the
    19	   author's decision on card `touchstone-reset-repro-pass`); the Mac gate keeps the tolerance criterion.
