    74	## 2. Estimand
    75	
    76	For rule r in {R3 (F111), C*, B3 (F000)}, fresh market m and churn rate p:
    77	
    78	g_p(r, m) = mean over the 200 evaluation seeds of the normalised gain of the D2+H3 attack selected by the registered
    79	search under churn p, against the rule's frozen truthful reference played under the same churn.
    80	
    81	Contrasts: d_p(m) = g_p(C*, m) - g_p(R3, m) and q_p(m) = g_p(B3, m) - g_p(R3, m), pooled with equal market weights, and
    82	their changes from the registered no-churn values on the same seeds. The attack and reference profits are reported
    83	separately. These are differences between finite searches with a fixed reference candidate in a changed environment, not
    84	identified optimal values. A weaker reference can raise a measured gain, and unequal reference losses can move either
    85	contrast in either direction.
