    87	## 3. Cells and execution contract
    88	
    89	- **Churn model.** Each of the nine honest opponents plays honest-max delivery and offer and, in each round, retires its
    90	  identity and re-enters under a fresh one with probability p (`docs/revision/churn/churn_v2.py` `HonestChurn`). The draw
    91	  uses the episode's `policy_seed[t, e]`, so it is deterministic and the same for every rule on the same seed. The model
    92	  keeps provider capacity and quality fixed and changes identity age; it also resets an honest provider's history and
    93	  lets it leave a false ban, so it does not isolate age information alone. **Rates p in {0.01, 0.05}** are illustrative
    94	  sensitivity settings without empirical calibration: mean identity lifetimes of 100 and 20 rounds, about 18 and 89
    95	  honest replacements per episode (measured, section 1). Whether the focal identity stays the newest is measured (section 4).
