   100	  frozen `revision_v2` stage functions through `_run_one` and reuses the reset driver's helpers
   101	  (`docs/revision/followup/reset_followup_v2.py`: input copies, pre-episode checks, follow-up freeze, acceptance,
   102	  comparators, inventory). `install()` wraps three `revision_v2` names, also in every pool worker's initialiser (tested):
   103	  `train_cell` (which `eval_cell` calls), so search, twin search, the doubling stage's reference menu, and evaluation run
   104	  under churn; `select_reference`, so a cell with churning opponents never reuses a candidate's stored no-churn training
   105	  profits (only the abstain candidate, whose profit is zero, keeps its value); and `reference_of`, so a churn job's
   106	  frozen reference carries its training-seed score evaluated under the same churn, which the doubling stage's
   107	  `reference_change` subtracts. Churn job ids carry the suffix `|churn<p>` so they never overwrite the copied registered
   108	  D2+H3 records that the reference menus read; each rate writes to its own directory (`results/v2/followup-churn/p<p>/`),
   109	  never to `eval/all`.
   110	- **References: frozen candidate, played under churn.** Each (market, rule) keeps its frozen truthful reference
   111	  candidate. Two reselections are distinguished. Reselecting among the frozen menu's candidates under churn needs only
   112	  their evaluation on the training seeds; the doubling stage does it for every cell (with the fix above), and its
   113	  `reference_change` is reported as a diagnostic, not as a bound on held-out bias. Regenerating the menus under churn
   114	  would need 60 D2+H3 and 60 X7-SC searches per rate, about 12.19 USD per rate before the churn slowdown (section 9); it
   115	  is not done.
